    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 green). Here's what I implemented for the structured address form, keeping the change as small and localized as possible.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added optional `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` string properties to `OwnerFields`, and removed `address` from the `required` list so structured-only requests bind without a 400. Because `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, both new fields are automatically echoed in the response DTO.\n\n**`StructuredAddress.java`** (new, small, zero surrounding complexity) \u2014 One static `apply` method: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` and the flat `address` via the existing `AddressNormalizer`, writes them back, then composes `address` = normalized line 1 (+ a single space + normalized line 2 when line 2 is present), preferring the structured fields and falling back to the flat `address` when no `addressLine1` is supplied. Returns the composed value.\n\n**`OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice.java`** \u2014 Replaced the two address lines in `validate` with a single call: `rejectIfBlank(errors, \"address\", StructuredAddress.apply(owner))`. This keeps the \"valid when address in either form, plus city\" rule (city is still rejected separately), so minimal legacy owners stay accepted.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with plain getters/setters so MapStruct maps them both ways and they persist.\n\n**`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql`** \u2014 Added the two columns at the end of `owners` and appended two trailing `NULL`s to the positional seed inserts (test DB uses `ddl-auto=none`; h2/mysql/postgres use `ddl-auto=update` and need no change).\n\n## How it satisfies the spec\n- Structured fields are preferred; the flat `address` remains accepted (both acceptance tests green).\n- Normalization applies to whichever fields are supplied.\n- Everything downstream that consumes the address reads the composed/normalized `address` (and the unchanged `city`/`postcode`), so household hash, postcode validation and locality use the structured values when present.\n- The response `address` is the composed `addressLine1` (+ space + `addressLine2` when present).\n\nThe mapper, controller, and all the read-side advice/aspects were left untouched \u2014 no edits to any large class beyond the four getter/setter additions on `Owner`.",
